Z||000013||Eric||11-06-1999||03:19 PM||||All this talk about power has got me thinking.  What power level is best for a street Fiero.  If you have 300 horsepower but only ever get to use half of it, does it really make sense?  I know the stock 2.8 needs a little help, but I can't see myself spending gobs of money in order to go a few tenths faster in the quarter.  From what I know, the best engine for the job is one that produces around 200 horsepower.  That is the same power output of a 3.1 rebuild which is also, the cheapest and easiest way to go.  My opinion may differ from some others, so if you think there's a better option out there please tell everyone what it is.||||reg||1
